  <description>
    The actual Spring Boot application: CoreApplication (main class), common/
    (GlobalExceptionHandler, WebConfig - cross-cutting glue nothing else depends
    on), and all of application*.yml + db/migration/** (Flyway discovers
    migrations by classpath location, so they live wherever the app that runs
    them lives). Depends on every other module - this is the one module that
    gets built into the executable jar (`mvn -pl app -am spring-boot:run` from
    core/, or `cd core/app` then `mvn spring-boot:run`). Still one process, one
    deployable - the modular monolith split changes compile-time boundaries
    between packages, not how this thing runs.
  </description>

